column21:
I can give many examples where I've handed code over and later there was problems due to less-skilled developers.<p>One good example I have is being called by a client who had a bug they couldn't fix in some code I had written years before. After looking into it, I found something like this:<p><pre><code>    // ABC 1/1/2001 removed this call as we don't understand why it was being called
    // x = performImportantCalculationABC();
</code></pre>
There are lots of terrible programmers out there. The average level of programming skills on HN is considerably higher than you'll find at most companies.<p>I've seen so much bad code written by people with senior job titles; confusing, ugly, inflexible, but working code.
